<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Bavaria-Ingolstadt</h1><p class="st-meta">1392 CE – 1447 CE · capital Ingolstadt</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Bavarian duchy ruled from Ingolstadt, best known for its brilliant and quarrelsome duke Louis the Bearded.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In the Bavarian partition of 1392 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stephen-iii-duke-of-bavaria">Stephen III</a> received the lands around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt">Ingolstadt</a>, scattered across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-bavaria">Upper Bavaria</a>. His daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isabeau-of-bavaria">Isabeau</a> married King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-of-france">Charles VI of France</a>, giving the house close ties with the French court.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Stephen's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vii-duke-of-bavaria">Louis VII the Bearded</a> spent years at the French court and returned with great wealth, building the New Castle and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liebfrauenmunster-ingolstadt">Church of Our Lady</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt">Ingolstadt</a>. He was constantly at war with his cousins in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landshut">Landshut</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> and was placed under the imperial ban. In 1443 he was captured in a conflict that involved his own son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-viii-duke-of-bavaria">Louis the Hunchback</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-viii-duke-of-bavaria">Louis the Hunchback</a> died in 1445 and his father in 1447 as a prisoner at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burghausen">Burghausen</a>, ending the line. The duchy passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-xvi-duke-of-bavaria">Henry XVI</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/duchy-of-bavaria-landshut">Duchy of Bavaria-Landshut</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ingolstadt">Ingolstadt</a> later became the seat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria's</a> first university, founded in 1472.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 1392 CE – 1447 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Germany and Central Europe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:87.40%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1392 CE – 1447 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ingolstadt</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Stephen III, Louis VII the Bearded</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Bayern-Ingolstadt</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1420&amp;focus=duchy-of-bavaria-ingolstadt" aria-label="Duchy of Bavaria-Ingolstadt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4944 475 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Bavaria-Ingolstadt lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5264 731L5279 723M5264 731L5282 737"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5279 723h0M5282 737h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5264 731h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5264 731h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ingolstadt. <a href="/atlas?year=1420&amp;focus=duchy-of-bavaria-ingolstadt">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
